{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$h''$ is the *second derivative* of $h$. In other words, it's the derivative of $h'$, which is the derivative of $h$.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $h''(x)$, we need to differentiate $h$ twice.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $h'(x)$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\nh'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[2^x\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\ln(2)2^x\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $h'$ to find $h''(x)$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\nh''(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\ln(2)2^x\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=[\\ln(2)]^22^x\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nh''(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\ln(2)2^x\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\ln(2)\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[2^x\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\ln(2)\\left(\\ln(2)2^x\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=[\\ln(2)]^22^x\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $h''(x)=\\big(\\ln(2)\\big)^22^x$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $h(x)=2^x$.\n\n**Find $h''(x)$.**\n\n$h''(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"0","simplify":false,"value":"\\ln2\\cdot\\ln2\\cdot2^{x}"},{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"1","simplify":false,"value":"\\left(\\ln2\\right)^{2}\\cdot2^{x}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra","logarithms"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
